			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-587204">
									

<p>Ideally, I think this was intended as a direct subversion of Xman type SCPs. The guy has metal wings. That sounds <em>awesome</em>. But… he can't fly, they can't be removed, and they trap him by anchoring him to concrete.</p>
<p>I see the idea.</p>
<p>But it's written in such a way that the blatant badfic potential is highlighted here, and I think that's part of the problem. The whole bit about the wings reacting to his mood, or blocking bullets? Yeh. Giving the wings an obvious benefit ruins the type subversion.</p>
<p>I almost like this SCP, and I'm glad it's up for edit, because with a few changes it <em>could</em> be a solid entry.</p>

